        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-15T09:59:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. Given that this feature might be one of the most complex part in NetworkStats.\nmaybe some javadoc will help people to understand the inputs/outputs without going through codes?\n\n2. I think this functions need refactor, there are 2 ideas about this, but I\u0027m not sure if they are helpful.\n2-1. Devide this function into 2:\n a) compute the \"total\" and outputs a new NetworkStats (or Entry[]).\n b) take output of (a) as input, and split across underlying ifaces, add to apps and output moved.\n\n2-2. Simplify it.\nTake computing for uid1 wifi rxbytes for example.\na) IIUC what you are doing can be shown by the following formula:\n uid1 wifi rxbytes \u003d uid1_tun_rxbytes * (MIN(underlying_total,tun_iface_total) / tun_iface_total) * (wifi_total / underlying_total)\n\nb) This can be devide into 2 cases, and reduce separately, where:\nb-1) if underlying_total \u003e tun_iface_total:\n uid1 wifi rxbytes \u003d uid1_tun_rxbytes * (wifi_total / underlying_total)\nb-2) if underlying_total \u003c tun_iface_total:\n uid1 wifi rxbytes \u003d uid1_tun_rxbytes * (wifi_total / tun_iface_total)\n\nc) Combine (b-1) and (b-2), you will get below:\n uid1 wifi rxbytes \u003d uid1_tun_rxbytes * wifi_total / MAX(underlying_total, tun_iface_total)\n\nThus, IIUC, by applying (c) you don\u0027t need 2 phases for this function.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1260,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 1260,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "5b0f5e213279870e65b81130e92c9b0708aafde5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
